	(483, 3, 45, NULL, 'Security Awareness Training Policy', '<h1>Security Awareness Training Policy</h1>
<h2>1. Purpose</h2>
<p>The purpose of this Security Awareness Training Policy is to establish the standards and procedures for enhancing cybersecurity awareness and resilience at Intellfence. This policy aims to systematically equip all personnel with the knowledge and skills required to protect the organization''s information assets, mitigate human-centric security risks, and ensure compliance with relevant regulatory frameworks and standards, including SOC 2 and ISO/IEC 27001.</p>
<h2>2. Scope</h2>
<p>This policy applies to all Intellfence employees, contractors, interns, temporary staff, and any third-party individuals who are granted access to Intellfence information systems, networks, or data. Participation in the mandated security awareness training program is a condition of initial and continued access to organizational resources.</p>
<h2>3. Policy Statement</h2>
<p>Intellfence is committed to fostering a robust culture of security through comprehensive, ongoing awareness training. The organization will implement and maintain structured training programs designed to educate the workforce on recognizing, preventing, and responding to cybersecurity threats. These programs will be regularly updated to address the evolving threat landscape and changes in regulatory requirements, thereby empowering personnel to act as a proactive line of defense in safeguarding company and customer data.</p>
<h2>4. Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<p><strong>4.1 Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) / Compliance Officer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Owns and is accountable for the overall security awareness training program.</li>
<li>Approves training curriculum, frequency, and content.</li>
<li>Reviews training metrics and reports on program effectiveness to senior management.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4.2 Human Resources (HR) Department</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Coordinates with the CISO to ensure new hires complete initial security training prior to or immediately upon commencement of employment.</li>
<li>Manages the integration of training completion records into personnel files.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4.3 Information Security Team</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Develops, updates, and delivers security awareness training content.</li>
<li>Manages the training platform and tracks participation and completion rates.</li>
<li>Conducts simulated phishing exercises and other security assessments.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4.4 Managers and Team Leads</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Ensure all team members under their supervision complete required training within defined deadlines.</li>
<li>Promote and reinforce security best practices within their teams.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>4.5 All Personnel</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Complete all assigned security awareness training within the stipulated timelines.</li>
<li>Apply the knowledge gained from training in their daily work activities.</li>
<li>Promptly report suspected security incidents or policy violations.</li>
</ul>
<h2>5. Policy Details</h2>
<p><strong>5.1 Training Requirements</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Initial Training:</strong> All new personnel must complete a foundational security awareness course within their first 30 days of employment or engagement.</li>
<li><strong>Annual Refresher Training:</strong> All personnel must complete an updated security awareness training course annually.</li>
<li><strong>Ad-hoc Training:</strong> Additional, targeted training may be required in response to specific security incidents, emerging threats, or changes in policy or technology.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>5.2 Training Content</strong>
Training content will cover, but is not limited to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Data classification and handling procedures.</li>
<li>Password hygiene and multi-factor authentication.</li>
<li>Recognizing and reporting phishing, social engineering, and other malicious attempts.</li>
<li>Safe internet and email usage practices.</li>
<li>Physical security and clean desk policies.</li>
<li>Incident reporting procedures.</li>
<li>Remote work security best practices.</li>
<li>Relevant compliance obligations (e.g., data privacy principles).</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>5.3 Measurement and Evaluation</strong>
The effectiveness of the training program will be assessed through:</p>
<ul>
<li>Training completion and pass rates.</li>
<li>Results from simulated phishing campaigns.</li>
<li>Analysis of security incident trends potentially linked to human error.</li>
<li>Periodic surveys to gauge security culture and knowledge retention.</li>
</ul>
<h2>6. Exceptions</h2>
<p>Requests for exceptions to any provision of this policy must be submitted in writing to the CISO for review and approval. Exceptions will only be granted based on a documented business justification, a formal risk assessment, and the implementation of compensating controls to mitigate any identified risks. All approved exceptions must be reviewed annually.</p>
<h2>7. Enforcement</h2>
<p>Compliance with this policy is mandatory. Failure to comply may result in corrective action, which can include, but is not limited to:</p>
<ul>
<li>Mandatory remedial training.</li>
<li>Restriction or revocation of system access privileges.</li>
<li>Formal disciplinary action up to and including termination of employment or contract, in accordance with Intellfence''s disciplinary procedures.</li>
<li>Legal or contractual consequences for third parties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>8. Definitions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Personnel:</strong> Refers collectively to all employees, contractors, consultants, temporaries, interns, and other workers at Intellfence.</li>
<li><strong>Information Assets:</strong> Any data, system, hardware, software, or service owned or used by Intellfence that stores, processes, or transmits information.</li>
<li><strong>Phishing:</strong> A fraudulent attempt to obtain sensitive information by disguising as a trustworthy entity in electronic communication.</li>
<li><strong>Social Engineering:</strong> Manipulative techniques designed to exploit human psychology to gain unauthorized access to information, systems, or physical locations.</li>
<li><strong>Security Incident:</strong> Any real or suspected event that compromises the confidentiality, integrity, or availability of Intellfence information assets.</li>
</ul>
