	(3, 1569, 'v1.1', '<h2>1.0 Purpose</h2>
<p>This Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) establishes the rules and guidelines for the appropriate and secure use of wefwefwefwe&#39;s information assets, including but not limited to networks, systems, software, data, and equipment. The purpose is to protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of corporate information, mitigate risks, ensure compliance with legal and regulatory obligations, and promote a secure and productive technology environment for all authorized users.</p>
<h2>2.0 Scope</h2>
<p>This policy applies to all individuals granted access to wefwefwefwe&#39;s information resources, including employees, contractors, consultants, temporary staff, interns, and any other third parties (collectively referred to as &quot;Users&quot;). It encompasses all company-owned or leased hardware, software, network infrastructure, data, cloud services, and communication systems, regardless of physical location or access method (e.g., on-premises, remote, mobile).</p>
<h2>3.0 Terms and Definitions</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Information Assets:</strong> Any data, system, hardware, software, or service that is owned, leased, or managed by wefwefwefwe that stores, processes, or transmits information.</li>
<li><strong>Authorized User:</strong> Any individual who has been formally granted access to company information assets for legitimate business purposes.</li>
<li><strong>Confidential Information:</strong> Any non-public, proprietary, or sensitive information belonging to wefwefwefwe, its customers, or partners, as defined in the Data Classification Policy.</li>
<li><strong>Incident:</strong> Any actual or suspected event that compromises the security, integrity, or availability of information assets.</li>
</ul>
<h2>4.0 Policy Requirements/Statements</h2>
<p>All Users are required to adhere to the following principles:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Authorized Use:</strong> Information assets are to be used solely for conducting official company business in accordance with assigned job responsibilities.</li>
<li><strong>Asset Protection:</strong> Users are responsible for safeguarding company assets under their control, including securing workstations when unattended and reporting lost or stolen devices immediately.</li>
<li><strong>Data Security:</strong> Confidential Information must be handled according to its classification level. Users must not attempt to access, copy, transmit, or destroy data without proper authorization.</li>
<li><strong>System Integrity:</strong> Users must not introduce malicious software, attempt to circumvent security controls, or engage in any activity that could degrade system performance or integrity.</li>
<li><strong>Respectful Conduct:</strong> Use of company resources for creating, transmitting, or storing harassing, discriminatory, obscene, or unlawful material is strictly prohibited.</li>
<li><strong>Compliance:</strong> All use must comply with applicable laws, regulations, licensing agreements, and other company policies.</li>
</ol>
<h2>5.0 Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Chief Information Security Officer (CISO):</strong> Responsible for the development, implementation, and overall governance of this policy.</li>
<li><strong>Information Technology (IT) Department:</strong> Responsible for implementing technical controls, monitoring compliance, and providing secure infrastructure in support of this policy.</li>
<li><strong>People Managers/Supervisors:</strong> Responsible for ensuring their team members understand and comply with this policy, and for addressing violations within their teams.</li>
<li><strong>All Users:</strong> Responsible for reading, understanding, and adhering to all provisions of this policy in their daily activities. Users must report any observed or suspected policy violations or security incidents immediately.</li>
</ul>
<h2>6.0 Procedures</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Access Provisioning:</strong> Access to information assets is granted following a formal request and approval process managed by IT, in alignment with the principle of least privilege.</li>
<li><strong>Secure Configuration:</strong> All company-managed endpoints must have approved security software (e.g., antivirus, endpoint detection and response) installed and kept updated.</li>
<li><strong>Password Management:</strong> Users must adhere to the corporate Password Policy for creating and managing authentication credentials.</li>
<li><strong>Incident Reporting:</strong> Suspected policy violations or security incidents must be reported immediately to the IT Help Desk or via the designated security incident reporting channel.</li>
<li><strong>Acceptance:</strong> All new Users must formally acknowledge receipt and understanding of this policy as part of the onboarding process.</li>
</ol>
<h2>7.0 Exceptions</h2>
<p>Requests for exceptions to specific policy requirements must be submitted in writing to the CISO or designated delegate. The request must include a detailed business justification, risk assessment, and proposed compensating controls. Exceptions are granted only under exceptional circumstances, for a limited duration, and require formal documented approval.</p>
<h2>8.0 Enforcement/Violations</h2>
<p>Violations of this policy may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment or contract, and/or legal action. The nature of the disciplinary action will be commensurate with the severity and intent of the violation, as determined by management in consultation with Human Resources and Legal departments. Activities that violate law may be reported to the appropriate authorities.</p>
<h2>9.0 Review/Approval</h2>
<p>This policy shall be reviewed at least annually by the CISO and updated as necessary to reflect changes in technology, business processes, or regulatory landscape. The latest approved version is the authoritative document.</p>
<p><strong>Policy Owner:</strong> Chief Information Security Officer
<strong>Approved By:</strong> [e.g., Chief Executive Officer / Board of Directors]
<strong>Initial Approval Date:</strong> [Date]
<strong>Next Review Date:</strong> [Date + 1 Year]</p>
<h2>10.0 References</h2>
<ul>
<li>Data Classification and Handling Policy</li>
<li>Information Security Incident Response Plan</li>
<li>Password Policy</li>
<li>Remote Access Policy</li>
<li>Relevant industry standards (e.g., ISO 27001, NIST CSF) and regulations.</li>
</ul>
